      "body": "> So, I would expect this code to fail with a TypeError in all cases.\n\nAnother option is using ``long_neg()`` directly, instead of abstract method.  This is the case for `int.__round__()`, for example:\n```pycon\n>>> class EvilInt(int):\n...     def __neg__(self):\n...         print(\"I'm a teapot.\")\n...         return 42\n...         \n>>> (-float(1 << 50) - 0.5) < EvilInt(-(1 << 50))\nI'm a teapot.\nTrue\n>>> round(123, EvilInt(-1))  # broken __neg__() is just ignored\n120\n```",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "pin": null,
