      "updated_at": "2025-12-22T19:14:42Z",
      "body": "> Another option is using `long_neg()` directly, instead of abstract method.\n\nI prefer this option. This code already uses `PyLong_GetSign()` and `_PyLong_Lshift()`. We need `_PyLong_Negative()` or `_PyLong_Absolute()`.  We should also ensure that `PyObject_RichCompareBool()` is not affected by the subclass behavior.",
