      "body": "@serhiy-storchaka, what about other methods?\n\nE.g. in the mentioned `int.__round__()` we use PyLong's internal methods on `ndigits` instance, which might be an int's subclass.  On another hand, math.integer's functions sometimes use Number Protocol functions (like PyNumber_Absolute or PyNumber_FloorDivide), which may (theoretically) trigger dunder methods in subclasses.\n",
